		zot:shortTitle "十八世纪海军领导的类型" ;
		zot:dateModified "2024-12-12T20:59:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
		zot:tags <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/b16cd58d-8b07-5b62-b816-19eb5f526c45> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/30c46492-b649-5d06-90c2-b40185122f1f> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/a3e1c1ec-4bab-5b44-b0dc-1f177df5a5c8> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/2fe02d96-f64b-5fdf-ba34-156d24dc1a92> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/2eef80c5-044f-5965-8e55-3cbf3712838a> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/f1188b33-b2aa-5bb5-bcb5-3199748af35e> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/05d3bc9a-8c82-5d49-bdfc-59a36dff4487> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/182f0082-d907-5e5f-8770-c749ec93c3d6> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/47d40135-3b89-5094-975f-0c2bde1c35e7> , <https://www.zotero.org/entities/tag/ccda80d7-e31c-50dd-8002-2a3281050217> ;
		zot:callNumber "0" ;
		zot:key "XFTZ6PEJ" ;
		zot:inLibrary <https://www.zotero.org/groups/open-access_history_books> ;
		zot:libraryCatalog "0" ;
		owl:sameAs <https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/31497> ;
		zot:abstractNote "The naval leader has taken centre stage in traditional naval histories. However, while the historical narrative has been fairly consistent the development of various navies has been accompanied by assumptions, challenges and competing visions of the social characteristics of naval leaders and of their function. Whilst leadership has been a constant theme in historical studies, it has not been scrutinised as a phenomenon in its own right. \n\nThis book examines the critical period in Europe between 1700 -1850, when political, economic and cultural shifts were bringing about a new understanding of the individual and of society. Bringing together context with a focus on naval leadership as a phenomenon is at the heart of this book, a unique collaborative venture between British, French and Spanish scholars. As globalisation develops in the twenty-first century the significance of navies looks set to increase. This volume of essays aims to place naval leadership in its historical context.\n\n【摘要翻译】在传统的海军史中，海军领袖一直占据着中心位置。然而，尽管历史叙事相当一致，各种海军的发展却伴随着对海军领导者的社会特征及其职能的假设、挑战和相互竞争的看法。虽然领导力是历史研究中的一个永恒主题，但其本身并没有作为一种现象受到仔细研究。\n\n本书探讨了1700-1850年间欧洲的关键时期，当时的政治、经济和文化变革带来了对个人和社会的新认识。本书的核心是将背景与海军领导力这一现象相结合，这是英国、法国和西班牙学者之间的一次独特合作。随着二十一世纪全球化的发展，海军的重要性将与日俱增。这本论文集旨在将海军领导力置于历史背景中进行研究。" ;
